0038:     Drop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.
0039: 
0040:     Input structure
0041:     - The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,
0042:       and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.
0043:     - A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous
0044:       bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.
0045: 
0046:     Rule
0047:     - Remove the top marker from its original cell.
0048:     - If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its
0049:       horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.
0050:     - If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row
0051:       with the marker color.
0052: 
0053:     Key insight
0054:     - The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop
0055:       column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.
0056:     """
0057:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0058:     assert g.ndim == 2
0059: 
0060:     bg = get_bg(g)
0061:     foreground_colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
0062:     assert len(foreground_colors) == 2, "expected marker and wall colors"
0063: 
0064:     singleton_colors = [color for color in foreground_colors if int(np.count_nonzero(g == color)) == 1]
0065:     assert len(singleton_colors) == 1, "expected exactly one singleton marker color"
0066:     marker_color = singleton_colors[0]
0067: 
0068:     wall_colors = [color for color in foreground_colors if color != marker_color]
0069:     assert len(wall_colors) == 1
0070:     wall_color = wall_colors[0]
0071: 
0072:     marker_coords = np.argwhere(g == marker_color)
0073:     assert marker_coords.shape == (1, 2)
